  "title": "Appetizer Shishito peppers",
  "description": "Minimal preparation for an excellent appetizer (or side dish).\n\nYou can serve them with soy sauce for dipping.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can find shishito peppers in your favorite grocery store. Prepare this super quick recipe in no time and your guests will love this delicious <a href=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/recipes/appetizers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">appetizer</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Did you know that 1 in 10 shishito peppers are really spicy?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":25765,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659306522216} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 25765-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Appetizer Shishito peppers</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/20210418_192112.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t<p>Minimal preparation for an excellent appetizer (or side dish).</p><p>You can serve them with soy sauce for dipping.</p>\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>6 oz Shishito peppers</li><li>a bit of olive oil</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li><p>In a saute pan heat olive oil over medium-high heat.</p></li><li><p>Add the shishito peppers and stir for 1-2 minutes, heating them up until they blister. Add salt and black pepper.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/IMG_0174.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Place the peppers on a paper towel to remove excess oil and serve.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/IMG_0176-150x150.jpg\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
